1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,500
You came all this way to tell me that?

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,500
I came because no one else would.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:11,000
The theater opens in twenty minutes.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,000
Then we don't have time for the polite version.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The projector they installed... it can do something new.

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,000
It can speak to the glasses. Directly.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Every caption, the instant the film speaks it.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
No devices to hand out. No closet full of broken screens.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,500
You're describing the end of my department.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,500
I'm describing the end of the waiting.

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
[audience laughter swells, then fades]

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,500
Did you hear that? The room laughed.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,500
And for once, everyone laughed together.

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
How far ahead does it send the words?

15
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:54,000
Three quarters of a second. The glasses hold them, then release.

16
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
On the exact frame. Like the film itself decided to speak.

17
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
And when the projectionist pauses?

18
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,000
The words pause too. They are married to the projector.

19
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
What about the Spanish screening on Friday?

20
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:14,000
Same film. Same booth. The glasses just choose Spanish.

21
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,000
[music rises, a single piano note holds]

22
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
You built this for your sister, didn't you.

23
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,500
I built it so she'd never have to ask again.

24
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Then let's open the doors.
